### Manual requests for the ComputeSeparation Aspire harness.
### The fake platform sends the platform requests: it assigns the pod on the WorkerProxy and links the worker to the Host.
###
### Run AppHost with the `project-manual` launch profile (F5, or the command below). It pins the ports used here and
### turns off automatic assign and link so you can send each step yourself, in order.
###
###   dotnet run --project tools\ComputeSeparation\AppHost\ComputeSeparation.AppHost.csproj --launch-profile project-manual

@platform = http://localhost:7060
@host = http://127.0.0.1:7071
@workerProxy = http://localhost:7081

### Expected flow, in order.

### 1. The Host has published its initial counts (0, 0).
GET {{platform}}/admin/infra/host/state

### 2. The platform assigns the pod on the WorkerProxy. Expect 201, or 204 if repeated.
### 503 WorkerNotReady means the sample worker has not connected yet; retry.
POST {{platform}}/fake/worker/assign

### Optional: the WorkerProxy pod state is now ReadyForRequest.
GET {{workerProxy}}/admin/worker/state

### 3. The platform links the worker to the Host. Expect 201, or 200 for a matching retry.
POST {{platform}}/fake/worker/link

### 4. The Host has published new counts (1, 1).
GET {{platform}}/admin/infra/host/state

### 5. A client invokes the function through Host -> WorkerProxy -> worker.
GET {{host}}/api/hello

### Test-only: clear history and accepted state.
DELETE {{platform}}/fake/history
